<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Virginia</h1><p class="st-meta">1607 CE – 1776 CE · capital Williamsburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">England's first lasting colony in America, founded at Jamestown in 1607, where tobacco, representative government and racial slavery took root together.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> Company of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> sent settlers to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-river">James River</a> in 1607, in the heart of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/powhatan-confederacy">Powhatan Confederacy</a>. Disease, hunger and conflict killed most early colonists, especially in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/starving-time">Starving Time</a> of 1609 to 1610. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-rolfe">John Rolfe's</a> sweet tobacco, first grown around 1612, gave the colony an export crop, and in 1624 the Crown took direct control.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 1619 the House of Burgesses met as the first elected assembly in English America, and the same year the first enslaved Africans arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-point-comfort">Point Comfort</a>. A planter elite grew rich on tobacco worked first by indentured servants and later by enslaved Africans, codified in the slave laws of 1705. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-england">Church of England</a> was established, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/college-of-william-and-mary">College of William and Mary</a> was founded in 1693. Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-berkeley-governor">William Berkeley</a>'s rule provoked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bacons-rebellion">Bacon's Rebellion</a> in 1676.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/williamsburg-virginia">Williamsburg</a> in 1699. Virginians such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patrick-henry">Patrick Henry</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a> led resistance to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, and in 1776 the colony adopted George Mason's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia-declaration-of-rights">Declaration of Rights</a> and became an independent commonwealth within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/colony-of-virginia.jpg" alt="Colony of Virginia" width="320" height="161"><figcaption>Image: Unknown engraver (from work by Lyon Gardiner Tyler) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Seal_of_Virginia_-_George_III.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1607 CE – 1776 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Williamsburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John Smith, William Berkeley, Lord Dunmore</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Virginia Colony, Dominion of Virginia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1692&amp;focus=colony-of-virginia" aria-label="Colony of Virginia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2760 836 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Virginia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3080 1092L3083 1087M3080 1092L4970 663M3080 1092L4997 651M3080 1092L4997 651M3080 1092L2570 1008"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3083 1087h0M4970 663h0M4997 651h0M4997 651h0M2570 1008h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3080 1092h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3080 1092h0"/></svg></a><figcapti